    <statement><p>Gravel is being dumped from a conveyor belt at a rate of
40 <m>{\rm ft}^3{\rm /min}</m>. It forms a pile in the shape of a right circular
cone whose base diameter and height are always the same.</p>
<p>How fast is the height of the pile increasing when the pile is 15 ft high?</p>
<p>The height is increasing at <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> ft/min.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.226354</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
